       30  Koulikoro Region ( Bambara : ߞߎߟߌߞߏߙߏ ߘߌߣߋߖߊ tr. Kulikoro Dineja) is a region in western Mali . It is the second administrative area of Mali and covers an area of 43,290 km 2 (16,710 sq mi). Its capital city is Koulikoro .
       31  Geography
       32  [ edit ]
       33  The region of Koulikoro is bordered by the regions of Nara and Nioro on the north, the region of Kita on the west, by Guinea and the region of Sikasso on the south, and by the regions of Ségou , Bougouni and Dioïla to the east. In 2023 the Koulikoro Region had a population of 2,224,418. These were m
       34  The region is irrigated by several rivers, including the Niger, Baoulé, Sankarani , Baogé, Bani and Bafing . The climate of the region's south has the high rainfall typical of the Sudan , while north of the Kita-Bamako axis, it tends to a Sahelian aridity.
       35  The largest cities of the region are Kati , Koulikoro , Kolokani , and Banamba ; however the most populous commune is Kalabancoro . The Boucle du Baoulé National Park and the natural reserves of Fina, Kongossambougou and Badinko shelter a diversity of wildlife.
