       73  [ edit ]
       81  Administrative subdivisions
       82  [ edit ]
       83  As of 2012 [update] the Koulikoro Region is divided into eight cercles , encompassing 29 arrondissements , 61 communes , and 1,218 villages. [ 4 ]
       84  The eight cercles are: [ 4 ]
       85  Koulikoro Cercle
       86  Banamba Cercle
       87  Kangaba Cercle
       88  Kati Cercle
       89  Kolokani Cercle
       90  Nyamina Cercle
       91  Siby Cercle
       92  Néguéla Cercle
       93  Mali's capital ( Bamako ) is located in the heart of the region, but forms a separate administrative entity called the Bamako Capital District; it is entirely surrounded by Kati Cercle.
