       71  The larger parts of Timbuktu and Goundam cercles (323,326 km² with about 134,000 inhabitants) were separated in 2016 to form the new Taoudenit Region . [ 8 ]
       72  Demographics
       73  [ edit ]
       74  The Tombouctou Region is the seventh most populated region in Mali, with a population of 974,278 in 2022. [ 9 ] With a total fertility rate at 4.9 births per woman, Tombouctou has a lower TFR than the Malian national average of 6.1 births per woman. [ 10 ]
